{
 "date": "2026-11-21",
 "what": "The Strix Halo figures on the project's page: prompt reading speed with zest against the GPU alone, and how far its answers are from the GPU's. Every row is the committed build. It replaces docs/results/halo-page-2026-11-19.json for the page's tables; that file keeps the earlier builds' runs, the one-token diagnosis and the NPU memory test.",
 "machine": "Ryzen AI MAX+ 395 / Radeon 8060S / XDNA2 NPU, 128 GB, Arch Linux (Omarchy), kernel 7.2.15 with its own amdxdna driver",
 "software": "llama.cpp b10944 Linux Vulkan release, unmodified; Mesa 26.2.5 (RADV); xrt 2.21.75-14, xrt-plugin-amdxdna 2.21.75-2; NPU power mode Default",
 "zest_build": {
  "libggml_zest_so_sha256_starts": "fea98a29f87d2ff2",
  "source": "commit 46443cf (the row split on by default, no 20 GB default limit on NPU weight copies on Linux)"
 },
 "speed": {
  "method": "tools/bench.py --rounds N --no-split: per round one process, `zest llama-bench -m MODEL -dev Vulkan0,XDNA0/Vulkan0 -p 2048 -n 0 -ub 2048 -b 2048 -r 3 -o json`, so the model loads once and the GPU-alone and with-zest figures sit next to each other in time; a round's ratio compares that pair; the row gives the median tokens a second over the rounds and the slowest and fastest round's ratio. 'split_off' is a second process per round with GGML_XDNA_SPLIT=0 (the NPU takes whole pieces and the GPU waits its turn), with a GPU-alone figure of its own.",
  "conditions": "Each model in a turn of its own holding the GPU and the NPU under both of the machine's schedulers. The rest of the machine was not held (the scheduler's whole-machine mode would have waited all day behind a server on a port), so each run checked the GPU was idle before starting and noted, every 3 s, any process other than the benchmark using more than half a core: 'other_work' is that record. Two rows ran with other work through them the first time (a terminal at a full core through Qwen3.5-9B, a 23-core job through Qwen3.6-35B-A3B) and were measured again once the processor was quiet; the disturbed runs are not here.",
